-- REQUEST accounts/UserBlock lookup has_blocked(blocker, blocked): blocked authors never reach the blocker's inbox or feed.
-- REQUEST organizations: transfer_recipients needs "members allowed to create repositories in an organization".
-- REQUEST repositories: a pull-mirror sync should emit per-ref MirrorSyncPushed(repository, ref_name, commits), MirrorRefCreated(repository, ref_name), MirrorRefDeleted(repository, ref_name) (distinct from code/PushReceived, attributed to the owner) — Forgejo keeps separate mirror_sync_* feed kinds.
-- REQUEST repositories: RepositoryStarred is listed as feeding the activity feed, but Forgejo records no star activity (star_repo is never produced); this module does not react to it.
-- REQUEST repositories: Watch.watch_issues / watch_pull_requests / watch_releases are used through repository_watchers(repo, category).
-- REQUEST issues: emit UserViewsIssue(viewer, issue) when a signed-in user opens an issue or pull request (web and API); provide Issue.subscribers / explicitly_unsubscribed, Comment.kind (comment | close | reopen | code | pull_push | review) for comment_mail_category; react to notifications/MailReplyReceived (create the comment as author, with the attachments) and notifications/MailUnsubscribeReceived (record an explicit unsubscribe).
-- REQUEST issues: IssueOpened is consumed for issues only (requires not is_pull); please confirm pulls never emits issues/IssueOpened for a PR, or the feed/inbox/mail would double up with pulls/PullRequestOpened.
-- REQUEST issues/pulls: IssueClosed / IssueReopened are consumed for both issues and PRs; pulls/PullRequestClosed / PullRequestReopened are therefore NOT consumed here — integration must ensure a PR close emits issues/IssueClosed (or switch this module to the pulls triggers).
-- REQUEST pulls: react to notifications/MailReplyReceived with replied_to_code set (reply in that code conversation); expose the mentions of a PR description, a review body and a code comment (issue_mentions / review_mentions / code_comment_mentions).
-- RESOLVED (integration): pulls emits both triggers for an auto-merge and sets
--   PullRequest.merged_automatically; the plain-merge rules here skip auto-merges.
-- REQUEST pulls: TeamReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, team) is not consumed; Forgejo notifies nobody per team member — confirm.
-- REQUEST actions/WorkflowRun.{status, notify_email, trigger_user, repository} and is_failure(status); decided (notifications 4): this module mails once per failed run attempt on WorkflowRunCompleted(run, prior_status) — not on WorkflowJobCompleted (supersedes actions' REQUEST about WorkflowJobCompleted; please update the "-- notifications mails the trigger user on failure" note in actions' Emits list to sit under WorkflowRunCompleted). WorkflowRunCompleted must fire once per attempt (prior_status non-final).
-- REQUEST actions: ScheduledWorkflowDisabledForInactivity(repository, workflow_file) is consumed (MailOnScheduledWorkflowDisabled mails the repository admins; no inbox thread, since threads are about issues or transfer offers).
-- REQUEST access: repository_admins(repository) = individual users with is_repo_admin(user, repository) (used for the workflow-disabled mail).
-- REQUEST issues: the thread audience (decided notifications 1) adds Issue.assignees; an explicit unsubscribe is read as issues/IssueWatch{user, issue, is_watching: false} (the inline mention / new-pull-request filters use it directly).
-- REQUEST repositories: MailOnCollaboratorInvited mails on CollaboratorInvited (decided notifications 5, answering repositories' REQUEST); MailOnCollaboratorAdded mails only for a site admin's direct add and tells it apart by doer.is_admin — an explicit `direct: Boolean` on CollaboratorAdded would be sturdier. Telling the inviter on acceptance / decline is not done.
-- REQUEST authentication: administration/UserPasswordSetByAdmin and UserPasswordSetByOperator revoke mail tokens here (decided notifications 3); if those resets should also send the password-changed mail, authentication should emit PasswordChanged(user) for them.
-- REQUEST federation: ActivityRecorded(activity) now fires exactly once per recorded activity (AnnounceActivity; there are no per-feed copies, decided notifications 6); the actor field is Activity.actor (not act_user), and Activity.is_private is gone — use activity.repository.is_private.
-- REQUEST federation: react to notifications/ActivityRecorded(activity) to publish to ActivityPub followers.
-- REQUEST authentication: react to notifications/SignOutPushed only if it needs to; the stream connection belongs here.
